### Get books WITH author details:
GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Books?$expand=author

### Get books WITH genre details:
GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Books?$expand=genre

### Get books with BOTH author and genre:
GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Books?$expand=author,genre

### Get an author WITH all their books:
GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Authors?$expand=books

### Get borrowings with book and member details:
GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Borrowings?$expand=book,member

### Get members with their borrowings AND the borrowed book:
GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Members?$expand=borrowings($expand=book)

### Filter books by a specific author:

GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Books?$filter=author_ID eq a1a1a1a1-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa

### Available books with calculated fields:
GET http://localhost:4004/reports/AvailableBooks

### Overdue borrowings with member contact info:
GET http://localhost:4004/reports/OverdueBorrowings

### Book pricing with GST calculations:
GET http://localhost:4004/reports/BookPricing

### Filter premium books only:
GET http://localhost:4004/reports/BookPricing?$filter=priceCategory eq 'Premium'

### Member activity:
GET http://localhost:4004/reports/MemberActivity?$filter=isActive eq true

### Without $expand — just the ID reference
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$select=title,author

### With $expand — full author details included
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$select=ID,title&$expand=author($select=ID,firstName,lastName)

### Cheapest books first (ascending is default)
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=price

### Most expensive books first
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=price desc

### Highest edition books first
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=edition desc

### Alphabetical by title
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=title

### Sort by genre, then by title within each genre
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=genre,title

### Published date newest to oldest
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=publishedDate desc

### Sort by multiple criteria with mixed directions
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=genre asc,price desc

### First groups by genre A-Z, then within each genre: most expensive first
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=genre asc,price desc

### First 2 books
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$top=2

### First 5 books, sorted by price
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=price&$top=5

### Page 1: First 3 items
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$top=3&$skip=0

### Page 2: Next 3 items
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$top=3&$skip=3

### Page 3: Next 3 items
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$top=3&$skip=2

### Top 3 most expensive books
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=price desc&$top=3

### Second page of results, 2 per page, sorted by title
GET http://localhost:4004/library/Books?$orderby=title&$top=2&$skip=2



### Filter Expression
1."Show me all products that cost more than $50" → $filter=price gt 50
2."Find customers from India" → $filter=country eq 'India'
3."Get all active employees" → $filter=isActive eq true
4."Show orders placed after March 2026" → $filter=orderDate gt 2026-03-31
5."Find books with 'Lord' in the title" → $filter=contains(title, 'Lord')
6."Products with stock between 10 and 100" → $filter=stock ge 10 and stock le 100
7."Authors from UK or USA" → $filter=country eq 'UK' or country eq 'USA'
8."Orders that are NOT delivered and cost over $500" → $filter=not (status eq 'Delivered') and totalAmount gt 500

### expand Practice
1. Get all books with their author name → GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Books?$expand=author($select=name)
2. Get all authors with their list of books (title only) → GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Authors?$expand=books($select=title)
3. Get orders with customer details and order items → GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Orders?$expand=customer,orderItems
4. Get products with supplier name and category name → GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Products?$expand=supplier($select=name),category($select=name)
5. Get the 5 most recent orders with items and product names → GET http://localhost:4004/Odata/v4/Catalog/Orders?$top=5&$orderby=orderDate desc&$expand=orderItems($expand=product($select=name))